<title>FRANCE: EU seen valuing early Mar French wheat around $151.</title>
<headline>EU seen valuing early Mar French wheat around $151.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>A European Union award of 398,500 tonnes of free-market soft wheat at a maximum refund of 12.90 Ecus per tonne values a tonne of early March French wheat at $151.33 per tonne, Reuters calculates.</p>
<p>The figure, which should be regarded as an estimate only, is based on benchmark standard-quality French milling wheat at Rouen and may vary significantly for other EU origins and types.</p>
</text>
